.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
env
# `env` above matches a path named exactly `env`, NOT `.env`. Without the two
# lines below, a developer's .env (encryption key, OpenSearch and Keycloak
# passwords, provider tokens) is eligible to be copied into an image. The
# backend Dockerfiles copy explicit paths today, so nothing leaks, but the
# images are published to a public registry and a broadened COPY must not be
# able to turn that into a leak.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
docker-compose.yml
*.md
.idea
.vscode
.claude
config/aicore_config.json
config/settings.json
config/chats/
*.bak
*.bak2
